<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%= render.call('head', title: site.name, description: site.summary, canonical: "#{site.url}/") -%>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= render.call('masthead') -%>

    <main class="land">
      <section class="hero">
        <div>
          <h1><span>Plain markdown in.</span> <span>A checked site out.</span></h1>
          <p class="summary">bearings turns the guides in your gem’s repo into a static site, a markdown copy of every page and llms.txt, then checks every link, anchor and example in them.</p>
          <%- featured = pages.find(&:featured) -%>
          <p class="actions"><a class="start" href="<%= featured.url %>">Start with <%= ERB::Util.h(featured.title) %></a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="pane">
          <figure>
            <figcaption>Two files to touch, one command to run</figcaption>
            <pre><i># Gemfile</i>
gem 'bearings'
gem 'rake'

<i># Rakefile</i>
require 'bearings/rake'
Bearings::Rake.install

<i># then build the site and check it</i>
$ bundle exec rake docs:check</pre>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="io" aria-label="What goes in and what comes out">
        <div class="pane">
          <p>You write</p>
          <figure>
            <figcaption>docs/GETTING_STARTED.md</figcaption>
            <pre><b># Getting started</b>

Install the gem, then run it.</pre>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <figcaption>docs-site/manifest.yml</figcaption>
            <pre>site:
  name: My gem
  url: https://docs.example.com

groups:
  - label: Start here
    pages:
      - source: docs/GETTING_STARTED.md
        slug: getting-started
        description: Install the gem and run it</pre>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p class="run">
          <code>$ bundle exec rake docs</code>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 56 32" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 16h50M40 5l12 11-12 11"/></svg>
        </p>
        <div class="pane">
          <p>bearings writes</p>
          <figure>
            <figcaption>_site/</figcaption>
            <pre class="site-tree">├── index.html
├── guides/
│   ├── <mark>getting-started/index.html</mark>  <i>the page</i>
│   └── <mark>getting-started.md</mark>  <i>its markdown copy</i>
├── <mark>llms.txt</mark>  <i>the index for agents</i>
├── search.json
├── sitemap.xml
└── robots.txt</pre>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <figcaption>_site/llms.txt</figcaption>
            <pre><b># My gem</b>

<b>## Start here</b>

- [Getting started](…/getting-started.md): Install
  the gem and run it</pre>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <h2>Then it checks what it built</h2>
      <p class="lead">Every link, anchor, code example, constant name, image and diagram in the guides. If the check passes, the site is correct.</p>
      <figure class="report">
        <pre><span class="cmd report-line">$ bundle exec rake docs:check</span><span class="report-line">docs/GUIDE.md:12: <b>[image]</b> shows an image with no alt text</span><i class="report-hint">describe the image in its alt text; it is all an agent or a screen reader gets</i><span class="report-line">docs/GUIDE.md:30: <b>[anchor]</b> links to `#instal`, but guides/guide/index.html has no id `instal`</span><i class="report-hint">point the fragment at an id on that page, such as a heading's</i></pre>
        <figcaption>Each problem names the file and the line to fix. A check that passes prints nothing.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>The guides</h2>
      <ol class="guides">
        <%- pages.each do |page| -%>
        <li>
          <a href="<%= page.url %>">
            <b><%= ERB::Util.h(page.title) %></b>
            <small><%= page.group_label %></small>
            <span><%= ERB::Util.h(page.description) %></span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <%- end -%>
      </ol>

      <footer class="foot">
        <span>Built by bearings from its own repo. The look is a template in docs-site/.</span>
        <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
        <a href="<%= site.repo %>">GitHub</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
